1. Calculate the total feed consumption per pig per day: Each pig eats 4 pounds of feed twice a day, so each pig eats 4 pounds * 2 = 8 pounds of feed per day. 2. Calculate the total feed consumption for all pigs per day: Dexter has five pigs, and each pig eats 8 pounds of feed per day, so the total feed consumption is 5 pigs * 8 pounds/pig = 40 pounds of feed per day. 3. Calculate the total feed consumption for all pigs per week: There are 7 days in a week, and the pigs consume 40 pounds of feed per day, so the total feed consumption per week is 40 pounds/day * 7 days = 280 pounds of feed per week. 4. Calculate the feed left after a week: Dexter ordered 300 pounds of feed and the pigs consumed 280 pounds of feed in a week, so the feed left is 300 pounds - 280 pounds = 20 pounds of feed.

The answer is 20.
\boxed{20}
